# Cyclops

## Lore

The Cyclops are an ancient race of one-eyed giants, said to have walked the Palladium World when the Old Ones ruled, by turns ferocious and civilized. They seem to have visited Earth in ancient times - the Greeks remembered them as demigods, and a Cyclops may be the root of the one-eyed Odin and of Thor''s lightning. With the Coming of the Rifts they walk the Earth again.

Their guarded secret is the making of magic lightning javelins and arrows, which they sell to kings, warlords, mercenary companies, dragons and wizards; even gods are said to trade favors for them, and the Splugorth of Atlantis keep several in their employ. Rumor says the Manistique Imperium has hired some to make lightning weapons for resale, and Northern Gun spies are trying to learn whether it is true. Little more than a hundred are believed to be on Rifts Earth.

**Alignment:** Any, but leans toward Anarchist and evil.

**Appearance:** Olive-skinned giants with one large eye in the center of the head, usually with long dark hair.

**Height:** 14 to 18 feet (4.2 to 5.5 m). **Weight:** 600 to 1,000 pounds (270 to 450 kg).

**Average Life Span:** 600 years.

## GM Notes

Cyclops are surprisingly civilized but aggressive toward smaller or weaker beings, greedy for wealth and prestige, fond of their own lightning weapons and of particle beam, ion and other high-tech gear. Traditional enemies are Titans, Changelings and Trolls; allies are Kobolds, Ogres, Jotan, Gigantes, Nimro and dragons, and they may deal with supernatural beings and creatures of magic. On Rifts Earth they are taken for monsters or D-Bees.
', 'published', 'data-script'
